--TEST--
`is void` and `is never` are refused, because no value inhabits either and the question has no answer rather than a knowable one (`rule:types/type-test`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The first of `rule:types/type-test`'s three refusals, and the one that
// says what "total" does not mean. `is` never refuses a test whose answer
// the declaration already settles — but `void` and `never` are not types a
// value can be *found* in, so there is nothing for the tag to compare
// against.
mixed $m = 1;
echo $m is void, "\n";
echo $m is never, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0811]: no value is ever a `void`, so `is void` has no answer
%A
error[E0811]: no value is ever a `never`, so `is never` has no answer
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
